  <content>
  <section><para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
<!--Do not edit this div tag.  It must surround the interaction block-->
<section class="check-understanding"><exercise data-content-id="c4f6daa0-50bc-428c-8cf5-7a097e999cc1"><problem><para>
      <para>1. Function \(f\) gives the temperature, in degrees Celsius, \(t\)<emphasis> </emphasis>hours after midnight. </para>
      <para>Choose which equation or expression represents the statement in function notation.</para>
      <para>The temperature was the same at 9 a.m. and at 4 p.m.</para>
      </para><para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\(f(9)=f(4)\)</para><para>\(f(9)=f(16)\)</para></problem><solution><para>\(f(9)=f(16)\)</para><para>
      <para>The correct answer is \(f(9)=f(16)\). </para>
    </para></solution></exercise></section></section>
</content>
